---
import PipelineFlow from './PipelineFlow.astro';
---

<section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open source · Apache-2.0 · Pre-alpha</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">AI agents inside your Nextflow pipelines. With evals and lineage.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      nf-agents is an open source toolkit for running AI agents inside Nextflow pipelines, with
      provenance and evals, in your own cloud account. The lineage tools are implemented on
      <code>main</code>, not yet released. Agent modules are planned for v0.2.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="#start">Try it in 5 minutes</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="#how">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="flow-figure">
    <PipelineFlow />
    <figcaption>
      Model answers are recorded once and replayed in tests, so no API key is needed. The
      lineage server is read-only.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 48px;
    padding-block: 48px 72px;
  }
  .hero-copy {
    flex: 1 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    color: var(--nf-muted);
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .flow-figure {
    flex: 1 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  figcaption {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--nf-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
